# The keypad under the kitty keyboard protocol's flag 1: a keypad key that
# makes text sends it, alone or with Shift, and is CSI number ; modifiers u
# with its own number under any other modifier; a keypad key that makes no
# text is always CSI number u, with NumLock among its modifiers; DECKPAM
# changes nothing.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Disambiguate escape codes, Functional key definitions
# covers: input.kitty-keyboard
size 20 2
send "\e[>1u"
key KP_1 mods=num char="1"
key KP_Add
key KP_Decimal char="."
key KP_End
key KP_Enter
key KP_Enter mods=num
key KP_Begin
key KP_Up
key KP_Insert
key KP_Delete
key KP_1 mods=ctrl
key KP_Add mods=alt
send "\e="
key KP_1 mods=num char="1"
key KP_End
key KP_Enter
